on must handle all edge cases.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Solution\n\n```python\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\n\ndef test_three_equal(a: int, b: int, c: int) -> int:\n    if isinstance(a, int) and isinstance(b, int) and isinstance(c, int):\n        if a == b == c:\n            return 3\n        elif a == b or b == c or a == c:\n            return 2\n        else:\n            return 0\n    else:\n        return 0\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Bash Command to Generate the File\n\nTo ensure the solution is properly set up and that the `mypy` checks pass, run the following command:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p experiments\necho "from typing import TYPE_CHECKING\\n\\ndef test_three_equal(a: int, b: int, c: int) -> int:\\n    if isinstance(a, int) and isinstance(b, int) and isinstance(c, int):\\n        if a == b == c:\\n            return 3\\n        elif a == b or b == c or a == c:\\n            return 2\\n        else:\\n            return 0\\n    else:\\n        return 0" > experiments/solution.py\n```\n\nThis will generate the required file `experiments/solution.py` with the correct implementation and type annotations.'
